Concrete places the TS SDK (and callers) still look protobuf-ish:

---

### 1. Duration WKT — almost every example

Usual would be `timeoutMs: 120_000`. Actual:

```20:20:examples/typescript/daytona/get-daytona-sandbox/src/main.ts
    timeout: duration(120_000),
```

Same pattern in essentially all TS examples for:

| Field | Example |
|-------|---------|
| `Config.timeout` | every `clientConfig()` |
| `lifetime.maximumLifetime` | `examples/typescript/modal/create-modal-sandbox/src/main.ts` |
| `lifetime.idleTerminate.after` | same + `create-modal-idle` |
| `lifetime.stoppedDelete.after` | `create-daytona-with-policies` |
| `provisioning.timeout` | `create-modal-ready` |

Helper admits it’s protobuf:

```142:145:sdks/typescript/sandbox/src/client.ts
/** Builds a protobuf duration for client configuration. */
export function duration(ms: number): Duration {
  return durationFromMs(ms);
}
```

(`Duration` ≈ `{ seconds, nanos }`, not `number`.)

Contrast: operation options already use ms:

```147:150:sdks/typescript/sandbox/src/client.ts
export interface OperationOptions {
  readonly signal?: AbortSignal;
  readonly timeoutMs?: number;
}
```

---

### 2. Wire `Config` still has `credentials: { case, value }`

Providers after `resolveClientConfig`:

```43:46:sdks/typescript/providers/daytona/src/mappings.ts
  const source = resolveClientConfig(config);
  const result = mapGeneratedClientConfig(source, environment);
  if (source.auth?.credentials.case === "bearerToken" && source.scope?.organizationId === undefined)
    configInvalid("scope.organizationId", "organization ID is required with bearer authentication");
```

Modal:

```40:45:sdks/typescript/providers/modal/src/provider_config.ts
  const credentials = source.auth?.credentials;
  if (credentials?.case === "tokenPair") {
    const mapped = mapTokenPairCredentials(credentials.value, "initialize");
  } else if (credentials?.case === "oauthRefresh") {
```

App authors using `ConfigInput` avoid this; anyone typing `Config` or reading materialize output does not.

---

### 3. Exported `SandboxSource` / `ReadinessProbe` still oneofs

```145:152:sdks/typescript/sandbox/src/sandbox_data_contracts.ts
export type SandboxSource = Omit<ProtoSandboxSource, "$typeName" | "kind"> & {
  kind:
    | { case: "providerDefault"; value: ProviderDefaultSource }
    | { case: "image"; value: ImageSource }
    | { case: "snapshot"; value: SnapshotSource }
    | { case: "warmPool"; value: WarmPoolSource }
    | { case: undefined; value?: undefined };
};
```

```190:198:sdks/typescript/sandbox/src/sandbox_data_contracts.ts
export type ReadinessProbe = Omit<
  ProtoReadinessProbe,
  "$typeName" | "check"
> & {
  check:
    | { case: "tcpPort"; value: number }
    | { case: "command"; value: CommandProbe }
    | { case: undefined; value?: undefined };
};
```

`CreateOptions` (what `Backend.create` takes) embeds those, not `*Input`:

```154:157:sdks/typescript/sandbox/src/client.ts
  create?(
    request: CreateOptions,
    options: OperationOptions,
  ): Promise<CreateResult>;
```

So provider code still branches on oneofs, e.g. Modal:

```71:71:sdks/typescript/providers/modal/src/mappings.ts
  if (request.source?.kind?.case !== "image")
```

---

### 4. Metadata oneofs (+ helpers that build them)

Public type:

```1200:1210:sdks/typescript/contracts/src/kit/sandbox/v1/sandbox_pb.ts
export type MetadataValue = Message<"kit.sandbox.v1.MetadataValue"> & {
  value: {
    value: boolean;
    case: "boolean";
  } | {
```

Runtime still constructs `{ case, value }`:

```46:51:sdks/typescript/sandbox/src/metadata_object.ts
function metadataValueFromPlain(value: MetadataPlain): MetadataValue {
  if (value === null) return create(MetadataValueSchema, {});
  if (typeof value === "boolean")
    return create(MetadataValueSchema, { value: { case: "boolean", value } });
  if (typeof value === "string")
    return create(MetadataValueSchema, { value: { case: "text", value } });
```

On create/info:

```230:230:sdks/typescript/sandbox/src/sandbox_data_contracts.ts
  providerOptions?: MetadataObject;
```

```247:247:sdks/typescript/sandbox/src/sandbox_data_contracts.ts
  providerMetadata?: MetadataObject;
```

Daytona maps provider metadata through the helper (internal), not plain JSON on the type itself.

---

### 5. Timestamp on `SandboxInfo`

```248:248:sdks/typescript/sandbox/src/sandbox_data_contracts.ts
  createdAt?: Timestamp;
```

Usual would be `Date`. Callers reading `info.createdAt` get WKT `{ seconds, nanos }` (examples mostly don’t print it yet).

---

### 6. Schema / wire APIs re-exported from the package

From `sandbox_data_contracts` (via `export *` in `index.ts`):  
`CreateOptionsSchema`, `ConfigSchema` (via client), `MetadataValueSchema`, `SandboxInfoSchema`, … — Buf message descriptors, not app-facing options.

Also materialize still builds wire oneofs:

```960:965:sdks/typescript/sandbox/src/client.ts
  return create(ConfigSchema, {
    ...rest,
    ...(auth === undefined
      ? {}
      : { auth: { credentials: authCredentials(auth) } }),
  } as MessageInitShape<typeof ConfigSchema>);
```

---

### 7. Dual timeout units (inconsistency users feel)

| API | Shape |
|-----|--------|
| `Client` / create timeouts on config & create options | `duration(ms)` → `Duration` |
| `OperationOptions.timeoutMs` | plain `number` |

Same “deadline” idea, two representations.

---

### 8. What examples already *don’t* lack

Nested auth/source (good):

```19:21:examples/typescript/daytona/get-daytona-sandbox/src/main.ts
    auth: { apiKey: { key: requireEnv("DAYTONA_API_KEY")  } },
```

Info field access is mostly normal (`info.id`, `info.state`, `info.origins`) — gaps there are mainly **Duration/Timestamp/metadata/oneof on types you don’t hit in happy-path examples**, not every `info()` call.

---

**Short inventory of “lacks”:** every `duration(...)` call site; wire `Config.auth.credentials`; exported `SandboxSource.kind` / `ReadinessProbe.check`; `MetadataValue` + `providerOptions`/`providerMetadata`; `createdAt: Timestamp`; public `*Schema` exports; `Backend`/`CreateOptions` still wire-shaped after materialize.

